content:
The primary member may cancel an active membership of Northgate Memberships; the cancellation is confirmed by the primary member, ends the membership and every card on it the same day, the Annual Reward balance is forfeited, and its refund is booked as one cancellation refund entry against the current year's renewal or new membership charge, returned to that charge's tender.

## Prerequisite clauses

The cancellation refund is fixed only after every add-on card fee of the current membership year whose card the primary member has removed carries a removal refund entry against that fee.

The cancellation refund is not worked out until, where a Plus guarantee claim request is dated within the current membership year, the current year's renewal charge carries its downgrade difference refund entry.

## What the confirmation records

Confirming the cancellation is the primary member's own action. One confirmation:

- records the member's confirmed cancellation request, dated that day;
- sets the membership to cancelled, with that day as its closing date;
- deactivates every card still in use on the membership;
- books the cancellation refund on the membership ledger against the stated fee charge for the stated membership year, returned to the stated tender.

Afterwards the membership shows as cancelled, none of its cards admit their holders, and the refund appears on the ledger.

## Invocation

The tool is `confirm_membership_cancellation_5b4de829`. It belongs to the member: member services unlocks it and hands it over, and the customer themselves runs it to confirm the cancellation of their own membership.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `membership_id` | the membership reference number being cancelled, as returned by the membership lookup and read out to the member | identifier |
| `source_txn_id` | the reference number of the current year's fee charge the refund is booked against, as returned by the membership ledger lookup | identifier |
| `term_end_date` | the last day of the current membership year | calendar date YYYY-MM-DD, local club date, never empty |
| `refund_amount` | the cancellation refund | USD with 2 decimal places, always positive; stored rounded half up to 2 decimal places as passed |
| `refund_reason` | the kind of refund booked | one of the reasons below |
| `tender` | where the refund is returned | one of the tender codes below |

`refund_reason` takes exactly one of:
  - `cancellation_full` — the current-year fees are refunded whole;
  - `cancellation_prorated` — only a share of the current-year fees is refunded;
  - `shortfall_guarantee` — never used on a cancellation, only for Plus guarantee refunds;
  - `downgrade_difference` — never used on a cancellation, only for the Plus premium refunded on a downgrade;
  - `duplicate_charge` — never used on a cancellation, only for a repeated charge;
  - `addon_card_removed` — never used on a cancellation, only for a removed add-on card's fee;
  - `not_applicable` — never used on a refund.

`tender` takes exactly one of:
  - `cash_or_debit` — back to the debit card or as cash when the charge was paid that way;
  - `northgate_visa` — back to the member's Northgate Rewards Visa card;
  - `northgate_store_card` — back to the member's Northgate Store Card;
  - `other_credit_card` — back to the other credit card the charge was paid with;
  - `shop_card` — onto a Northgate Shop Card;
  - `reward_certificate` — never used for a refund destination, only for charges paid with a certificate;
  - `not_applicable` — never used for a refund, only for entries that carry no payment.

## Return

A text receipt reading "Cancellation confirmed", followed by the refund entry reference on the membership ledger, the membership reference, the refund amount in USD with 2 decimals, the refund reason, the tender, the number of cards deactivated (a whole number) and the status "cancelled". A receipt starting "Cancellation confirmed" means the cancellation, the card deactivations and the refund are all recorded.
